# Force LF regardless of local git config (core.autocrlf) or OS. Without
# this, a Windows working tree can silently end up with CRLF line endings
# that a raw `tar` deploy (not `git archive`) ships as-is to the Linux
# server — harmless for most text, but fatal for run.sh: a CRLF-terminated
# "#!/bin/bash\r" shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally
# named "/bin/bash\r", which doesn't exist. This broke production once
# (2026-08-20) after a bulk edit reintroduced CRLF; fixed at the root here
# instead of relying on remembering to check every time.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
